## The one rule that matters

Server state belongs to React Query (`hooks/`); the Zustand store holds **UI**
state — filters, selection, open dialogs. Mirroring fetched rows into the store
is the failure this split exists to prevent: two copies, one stale.

## Import boundary

```ts
import { {{ ModuleId }}List, use{{ ModuleId }}List } from '@/lib/{{ module_id }}';
```

Reaching past the barrel (`@/lib/{{ module_id }}/components/...`) couples callers
to the internal layout and is rejected by the Nx boundary tags
(`docs/architecture/frontend/standards/react-nx-boundaries.md`).

## Server vs Client components

`components/` are Client Components (`'use client'`) because they hold state and
handlers. Pages under `app/` stay Server Components and pass data down; see
`docs/architecture/frontend/standards/react-conventions.md`.
